    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d129">

                <pb facs="0243" n="897" sameAs="frus:frus1875v02/pg897"/>

                <head>No. 428.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish to Mr. Foster.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1875-04-13"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 13,
                        1875</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 213.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I transmit a copy of a letter of the 7th
                    instant and its inclosure addressed to this Department by the Secretary of War
                    upon the subject <pb facs="0244" n="898" xml:id="pg898"/> of depredations in
                    Texas by Indians from Mexico. The facts stated in the communication tend to
                    confirm the impressions of the Department which have already been conveyed to
                    you as to the impolicy on the part of the Mexican government to keep within
                    their territory Indians properly belonging to the United States.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed></closer>





